{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isMatching(_:)","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isMaximalMatching(_:)","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPerfectMatching(_:)","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalMatching()","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumBipartiteMatching(bipartition:)","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumMatching()","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-6l4u0","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-8dxpn","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumWeightFullMatching(bipartition:weight:)","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumWeightMatching(weight:)-1lg3b","doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumWeightMatching(weight:)-4rzlr"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","role":"symbol","title":"Graph","modules":[{"name":"MatchingModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"extension","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14MatchingModuleE014_maximumWeightC0_8searched8reported0E11Cardinality4halfAD0C0Vyxqd__GAD01_cA0V_Sayqd__GAOSbqd__qd__XEtSLRd__s13SignedNumericRd__lF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumMatching()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum-cardinality matching by Edmonds’ blossom algorithm: for each still-free vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, a breadth-first alternating search (rows in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order) that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contracts blossoms and augments along the first free vertex found, skipping the vertices of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier failed searches. The matching returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this procedure’s, a documented function of the vertex order and rows. Parallel edges: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy met first. Vertices of a search that fails are skipped by later searches. O(n · m · log n)."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumMatching()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Matching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","title":"maximumMatching()","url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximummatching()"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"MatchingModule","url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-6l4u0":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum-weight matching (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"max_weight_matching"},{"type":"text","text":", the same matching): Galil’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"primal–dual blossom algorithm in Van Rantwijk’s formulation, with NetworkX’s iteration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders. With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumCardinality"},{"type":"text","text":", the heaviest among the maximum-cardinality matchings;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without it, a negative edge is never taken and a zero-weight one may be. Parallel edges: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heaviest copy (the earliest on ties). Self-loops are never weighed; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per other edge, in position order. Exact. O(n³)."}],"title":"maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)","url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumweightmatching(weight:maximumcardinality:)-6l4u0","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumWeightMatching","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumCardinality","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","text":"Matching","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-6l4u0"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumWeightMatching(weight:)-1lg3b":{"url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumweightmatching(weight:)-1lg3b","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The least weight among the maximum-cardinality matchings (NetworkX "},{"code":"min_weight_matching","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"):"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumWeightMatching","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"maximumCardinality","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on (1 + the greatest weight) − w, reporting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the original weights’ sum. Parallel edges: the lightest copy (the earliest on ties)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops are never weighed and the vertex order is kept (NetworkX weighs loops for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greatest weight and rebuilds the graph from its edges). O(n³)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumWeightMatching(weight:)-1lg3b","type":"topic","title":"minimumWeightMatching(weight:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumWeightMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","text":"Matching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtoc